{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "VeloRix Tournaments Public API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "summary": "Read-only JSON API for VeloRix Tournaments, an India-focused Free Fire and BGMI mobile esports tournament platform.",
    "description": "Public, unauthenticated, read-only endpoints exposing VeloRix Tournaments content: published pages (tournaments, announcements, policies), the current Android APK release and live site status.\n\n## Errors\nEvery non-2xx response is `application/problem+json` (RFC 9457) using the `Error` schema: a `type` URI, a machine-readable `title`/`error.code`, the HTTP `status`, a human-readable `error.message` and an actionable `error.hint`. Error codes are enumerated in `Error.error.code`, so agents can branch on them without parsing prose.\n\n## Rate limits\nEvery response carries RFC 9331 style rate-limit headers: `RateLimit-Policy`, `RateLimit`, plus the legacy `X-RateLimit-Limit` / `X-RateLimit-Remaining` / `X-RateLimit-Reset` mirrors. The default policy is 120 requests per 60 second window per client IP. When exhausted the API returns `429` with `Retry-After` (seconds) and the `rate_limited` error code. Agents should self-throttle from `RateLimit` rather than retrying blindly.\n\n## Versioning and deprecation\nThe API is versioned in the URL path (`/api/v1`). Breaking changes ship as a new path segment (`/api/v2`); the previous version stays available for at least 180 days. A version scheduled for removal returns `Deprecation` (RFC 9745) and `Sunset` (RFC 8594) headers on every response, plus a `Link; rel=\"deprecation\"` pointing at the policy at https://velorix-hub.vercel.app/md/versioning.md. Every response also carries `X-API-Version`. Full policy: https://velorix-hub.vercel.app/md/versioning.md",
    "termsOfService": "https://velorix-hub.vercel.app/terms",
    "contact": {
      "name": "VeloRix Tournaments",
      "email": "service.veloxyra@gmail.com",
      "url": "https://velorix-hub.vercel.app/developers"
    },
    "license": {
      "name": "Proprietary \u2014 content reusable with attribution",
      "url": "https://velorix-hub.vercel.app/ai.txt"
    }
  },
  "externalDocs": {
    "description": "VeloRix developer and agent resources (MCP server, OpenAPI, rate limits, versioning policy)",
    "url": "https://velorix-hub.vercel.app/developers"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://velorix-hub.vercel.app/api/v1",
      "description": "Production (v1)"
    }
  ],
  "x-rate-limit": {
    "policy": "120 requests per 60 second window per client IP",
    "headers": [
      "RateLimit-Policy",
      "RateLimit",
      "Retry-After",
      "X-RateLimit-Limit",
      "X-RateLimit-Remaining",
      "X-RateLimit-Reset"
    ],
    "documentation": "https://velorix-hub.vercel.app/md/versioning.md#rate-limits"
  },
  "x-versioning": {
    "scheme": "url-path",
    "current": "v1",
    "deprecationHeaders": [
      "Deprecation",
      "Sunset",
      "Link"
    ],
    "minimumSupportWindowDays": 180,
    "policy": "https://velorix-hub.vercel.app/md/versioning.md"
  },
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "pages",
      "description": "Published VeloRix pages: tournaments, announcements, policies."
    },
    {
      "name": "releases",
      "description": "VeloRix Android application releases."
    },
    {
      "name": "platform",
      "description": "Platform metadata and live status."
    }
  ],
